{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790995898,"nonce":"Y2vv6PbOSSE3i/Gvk63xp7HOTlw=","title":"Float32x4.splat allocates when inlined into a large caller","message":"Reported by the ChimpMonk physics session, measured at ash 1210987 (AOT and `--mode jit`, `ASH_GC_TLAB=0`).\n\nChimpMonk's `SimdBatch.integrateBodies` is Haxe-inline and lands inside the large `World.stepSegment`. It called `Float32x4.splat` five times per call, and each splat allocated a 16-byte vector: 320 GC bytes per `World.step` on an empty world (4 segments x 5 splats x 16). The same code with the constants written to a scratch `hl.Bytes` and read with `Float32x4.load` allocates nothing. A small standalone caller does not allocate, so this looks caller-size dependent, like the earlier inline/SROA growth-cap cases (see 1c26b13).\n\n**Reproducer.** Build ChimpMonk at two commits of its repository with the driver below, link with `ash --build`, run each binary with `ASH_GC_TLAB=0`:\n\n```\nhaxe -L hashlink --class-path \u003cash\u003e/haxelib/ash-simd --class-path \u003cchimpmonk@rev\u003e --class-path . \\\n  -D ash_simd=1 -D ash_simd_no_hdll -main EmptyStep -hl empty-\u003crev\u003e.hl\nash --build empty-\u003crev\u003e empty-\u003crev\u003e.hl \u0026\u0026 ASH_GC_TLAB=0 ./empty-\u003crev\u003e\n```\n\n- fb1bd5a (splat): 1000 empty steps, 320,160 bytes\n- 115c979 (load from scratch): 1000 empty steps, 160 bytes (the 160 is two stats() reads)\n\nEmptyStep.hx:\n\n```haxe\nimport chimpmonk.geom.ShapeBuilder;\nimport chimpmonk.physics.core.World;\nimport chimpmonk.physics.core.Handles.BodyType;\n\nclass EmptyStep {\n\tstatic function main():Void {\n\t\tvar world = new World(16, 16);\n\t\tfor (_ in 0...10) world.step(1.0 / 60.0);\n\t\tvar before = hl.Gc.stats().totalAllocated;\n\t\tfor (_ in 0...1000) world.step(1.0 / 60.0);\n\t\tvar empty = hl.Gc.stats().totalAllocated - before;\n\t\tvar ball = world.createBody(BodyType.Dynamic, 0, 0);\n\t\tworld.attachShape(ball, ShapeBuilder.makeCircle(0.2));\n\t\tfor (_ in 0...10) world.step(1.0 / 60.0);\n\t\tbefore = hl.Gc.stats().totalAllocated;\n\t\tfor (_ in 0...1000) world.step(1.0 / 60.0);\n\t\tvar falling = hl.Gc.stats().totalAllocated - before;\n\t\tbefore = hl.Gc.stats().totalAllocated;\n\t\tvar probe = hl.Gc.stats().totalAllocated - before;\n\t\tSys.println('1000 empty steps: $empty bytes; 1000 steps with one falling ball: $falling bytes; stats probe: $probe');\n\t}\n}\n```\n\nThe original files were in chimpmonk's session scratchpad (ash-report/, with SplatRepro.hx as the small clean caller), which is temporary.","files":null}]}